</DataGrid.Columns></DataGrid>
<Border Background="#151622" CornerRadius="9" Padding="12" Margin="0,12,0,0"><StackPanel>
<TextBlock Name="SensorHistoryTitle" Text="Select a sensor row to inspect its history." Foreground="#D8C8FF" FontSize="16"/>
<TextBlock Name="SensorHistoryScale" Foreground="#929BB5" Margin="0,4"/>
<Viewbox Height="150" Stretch="Fill"><Canvas Name="SensorHistoryChart" Width="800" Height="150" Background="#10111A" ClipToBounds="True"/></Viewbox>
<TextBlock Name="SensorHistoryTime" Foreground="#929BB5" Margin="0,8,0,0"/>
</StackPanel></Border></StackPanel></ScrollViewer></Grid></TabItem>
   <TabItem Header="Optimize" Tag="&#xE713;"><ScrollViewer VerticalScrollBarVisibility="Auto"><StackPanel Margin="20"><TextBlock Foreground="#EFF0FA" Text="Choose a supported change" FontSize="22"/><TextBlock Foreground="#B0B5CC" Text="Windows power plans are available in this preview. They can affect responsiveness, heat, battery life and sleep behaviour. They do not overclock or undervolt your hardware. No improvement is guaranteed."/><Button Name="PlansRefresh" Content="Load installed power plans" HorizontalAlignment="Left"/><ComboBox Name="Plans" DisplayMemberPath="Name" Margin="0,8" Padding="10"/><WrapPanel><Button Name="Apply" Content="Review and apply"/><Button Name="Restore" Content="Restore previous plan"/></WrapPanel><TextBlock Name="PowerStatus" Foreground="#A786FF" Text="No changes made."/><Border Background="#202034" Padding="18" Margin="0,20,0,0"><StackPanel><TextBlock Foreground="#EFF0FA" FontSize="18" Text="GPU power limits: see Tuning"/><TextBlock Foreground="#B0B5CC" Text="CPU overclocking / undervolting: unavailable&#10;GPU clock offsets: NVIDIA preview on Tuning; voltage controls unavailable&#10;RAM timings / XMP / EXPO: guidance only&#10;Fan control and BIOS writes: unavailable&#10;&#10;Support will require vendor-specific integrations and testing on the actual hardware. There are no hidden tuning writes or automatic startup profiles."/></StackPanel></Border></StackPanel></ScrollViewer></TabItem>
   <TabItem Header="CPU tuning" Tag="&#xE950;"><ScrollViewer VerticalScrollBarVisibility="Auto"><StackPanel Margin="20">
    <TextBlock Text="CPU tuning readiness" FontSize="24" FontWeight="SemiBold"/>
    <TextBlock Text="Check your hardware and record a CPU baseline. Direct CPU overclocking, undervolting and power-limit writes are not available in this version." Foreground="#B0B5CC"/>
    <WrapPanel><Button Name="CpuReadinessScan" Content="Scan CPU and motherboard"/><Button Name="CpuBaselineRun" Content="Run CPU baseline · 3 tests" IsEnabled="False"/><Button Name="CpuReadinessExport" Content="Export readiness report" IsEnabled="False"/><Button Name="CpuVendorHelp" Content="Vendor requirements" IsEnabled="False"/></WrapPanel>
    <Border Style="{StaticResource Card}"><TextBlock Name="CpuReadinessText" TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="Scan PC to collect hardware inventory."/></Border>
    <Border Style="{StaticResource Card}"><StackPanel><TextBlock Text="Controls and availability" FontSize="20"/><ItemsControl Name="CpuControlTable" Margin="0,12,0,0"><ItemsControl.ItemTemplate><DataTemplate><Border BorderBrush="#33415E" BorderThickness="0,0,0,1" Padding="0,10"><Grid><Grid.ColumnDefinitions><ColumnDefinition Width="1.1*"/><ColumnDefinition Width="1.3*"/><ColumnDefinition Width="2*"/></Grid.ColumnDefinitions><TextBlock Text="{Binding Control}" FontWeight="SemiBold" Margin="0,0,12,0"/><TextBlock Grid.Column="1" Text="{Binding Availability}" Foreground="#B39CFF" Margin="0,0,12,0"/><TextBlock Grid.Column="2" Text="{Binding Detail}" Foreground="#B0B5CC" Margin="0"/></Grid></Border></DataTemplate></ItemsControl.ItemTemplate></ItemsControl></StackPanel></Border>
    <Border Style="{StaticResource Card}"><StackPanel><TextBlock Text="Baseline workflow" FontSize="20"/><TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="1. Scan your PC. Save work and keep background activity consistent.&#10;2. Run the three-test CPU baseline; temperature checks are performed by the workload.&#10;3. Open Repeated results for median and variation, and Test results for temperatures.&#10;&#10;An unlocked-style name does not prove that the board, BIOS or driver permits CPU tuning. This page does not apply settings, establish safe offsets, or restore changes made in BIOS or another app." Foreground="#B0B5CC"/></StackPanel></Border>
   </StackPanel></ScrollViewer></TabItem>
   <TabItem Header="Tuning" Tag="&#xE9E9;"><ScrollViewer VerticalScrollBarVisibility="Auto"><StackPanel Margin="20">
    <TextBlock Text="Measure. Review. Apply. Compare." FontSize="24" FontWeight="SemiBold"/>
    <TextBlock Text="Start with a compatibility check and baseline. Supported NVIDIA controls include power-limit reductions and manual P0 clock offsets. Voltage changes and BIOS writes are not available." Foreground="#B0B5CC"/>
    <WrapPanel><Button Name="DetectTuning" Content="Detect compatibility"/><Button Name="SaveBaseline" Content="Save baseline" Background="#28233D" IsEnabled="False"/><Button Name="CompareBaseline" Content="Compare with baseline" Background="#28233D"/></WrapPanel>
    <Border Style="{StaticResource Card}"><TextBlock Name="CapabilityText" Text="Compatibility has not been checked. Readable power limits do not guarantee permission to change them."/></Border>
    <Border Style="{StaticResource Card}"><StackPanel><TextBlock Text="GPU power limit" FontSize="20"/>
     <ComboBox Name="GPUDevice" DisplayMemberPath="Label" Margin="0,8" Padding="10"/>
     <ComboBox Name="PowerPreset" SelectedIndex="0" Margin="0,8" Padding="10"><ComboBoxItem Tag="90" Content="90% of original power limit"/><ComboBoxItem Tag="80" Content="80% of original power limit"/></ComboBox>
     <TextBlock Text="Presets below the GPU minimum or above the current limit are rejected. Restore first to move back up. No settings change until you review and apply. Changes may persist after closing; restore is explicit." Foreground="#929BB5"/>
     <WrapPanel><Button Name="ApplyGPU" Content="Review and apply GPU limit"/><Button Name="RestoreGPU" Content="Restore saved GPU limit" Background="#28233D"/></WrapPanel><TextBlock Name="TuningStatus" Text="No GPU changes made in this session." Foreground="#B195FF"/>
    </StackPanel></Border>
    <Border Style="{StaticResource Card}"><StackPanel>
     <TextBlock Text="GPU overclocking · NVIDIA preview" FontSize="20"/>
     <TextBlock Text="Manual graphics and memory offsets for performance state P0. Values use the driver's MHz units; memory offsets are not advertised effective memory speed. Support depends on your GPU and driver. AMD/Intel controls are not implemented." Foreground="#B0B5CC"/>
     <Button Name="DetectClocks" Content="Detect clock support" HorizontalAlignment="Left"/>
     <ComboBox Name="ClockGPU" DisplayMemberPath="Label" Margin="0,8" Padding="10"/>
     <TextBlock Name="ClockInfo" Text="Clock support has not been checked."/>
     <WrapPanel><StackPanel Margin="0,0,20,0"><TextBlock Text="Core offset (MHz)"/><TextBox Name="CoreOffset" IsReadOnly="False" IsEnabled="False" MaxLength="11" Width="160" BorderBrush="#51436F" BorderThickness="1" AutomationProperties.Name="Core clock offset in MHz"/></StackPanel><StackPanel><TextBlock Text="Memory offset (MHz)"/><TextBox Name="MemoryOffset" IsReadOnly="False" IsEnabled="False" MaxLength="11" Width="160" BorderBrush="#51436F" BorderThickness="1" AutomationProperties.Name="Memory clock offset in MHz"/></StackPanel></WrapPanel>
     <TextBlock Text="Enter the desired offset, not an increment. Applying requires administrator access and a current GPU temperature below 85 C. Readback confirms the setting, not stability. Use a small change and compare equivalent tests. No automatic voltage, power-limit or startup changes." Foreground="#929BB5"/>
     <WrapPanel><Button Name="ApplyClocks" Content="Review and apply offsets" IsEnabled="False"/><Button Name="RestoreClocks" Content="Restore saved clock offsets" Background="#28233D" IsEnabled="False"/></WrapPanel>
     <TextBlock Name="ClockStatus" Text="No clock changes made. Changes may remain after closing the app; restore is explicit." Foreground="#B195FF"/>
    </StackPanel></Border>
    <Border Style="{StaticResource Card}"><StackPanel><TextBlock Text="Guided core trial" FontSize="20"/>
    <TextBlock Text="Three baseline runs, one reviewed +15 MHz core change, then three retests. Memory stays unchanged. This measures one candidate; it does not scan for a maximum overclock or certify stability." Foreground="#B0B5CC"/>
    <WrapPanel><Button Name="CoreTrialStart" Content="1. Record baseline"/><Button Name="CoreTrialApply" Content="2. Review and retest" IsEnabled="False"/></WrapPanel>
    <WrapPanel><Button Name="CoreTrialKeep" Content="Keep trial offsets" IsEnabled="False"/><Button Name="CoreTrialRestore" Content="Restore original offsets" IsEnabled="False" Background="#28233D"/><Button Name="CoreTrialCancel" Content="Cancel / restore" IsEnabled="False" Background="#28233D"/></WrapPanel>
    <TextBlock Name="CoreTrialStatus" Text="Start with Scan PC and Detect clock support." Foreground="#B195FF"/>
    </StackPanel></Border>
    <Border Style="{StaticResource Card}"><StackPanel><TextBlock Text="Before / after" FontSize="20"/><TextBlock Name="BaselineResult" Text="Save a baseline containing a complete three-run batch. Repeat the same batch after a reviewed change. Comparisons require three matching successful runs on each side."/></StackPanel></Border>
   </StackPanel></ScrollViewer></TabItem>
   <TabItem Header="Repeated results" Tag="&#xE9D9;"><Grid Margin="20"><TextBox Name="BatchReport" Text="Start a three-run batch from Benchmark. Median and spread will appear here."/></Grid></TabItem>
   <TabItem Header="Profiles" Tag="&#xE8B7;"><ScrollViewer VerticalScrollBarVisibility="Auto"><StackPanel Margin="20"><TextBlock Text="Named comparison baselines" FontSize="24" FontWeight="SemiBold"/><TextBlock Text="Keep separate baselines for different experiments. A profile is a saved copy of the active baseline, including its readings and reported settings. Loading it never applies hardware settings." Foreground="#B0B5CC"/>
    <Border Style="{StaticResource Card}"><StackPanel><TextBlock Text="Save the active baseline" FontSize="20"/><TextBlock Text="First use Tuning → Save baseline. Then give that baseline a name here." Foreground="#929BB5"/><TextBox Name="ProfileName" IsReadOnly="False" MaxLength="60" Text="Original settings" BorderBrush="#51436F" BorderThickness="1"/><Button Name="SaveProfile" Content="Save named profile" HorizontalAlignment="Left"/></StackPanel></Border>
    <Border Style="{StaticResource Card}"><StackPanel><TextBlock Text="Saved profiles" FontSize="20"/><ComboBox Name="ProfilePicker" DisplayMemberPath="Label" Padding="10" Margin="0,8"/><Button Name="LoadProfile" Content="Load for comparison" HorizontalAlignment="Left"/><TextBlock Name="ProfileStatus" Text="No profile loaded this session. Results and profiles are stored locally." Foreground="#B195FF"/></StackPanel></Border>
   </StackPanel></ScrollViewer></TabItem>
   <TabItem Header="Updates" Tag="&#xE895;"><ScrollViewer VerticalScrollBarVisibility="Auto"><StackPanel Margin="20">
<TextBlock Text="App updates" FontSize="24"/><TextBlock Name="InstalledVersion" Text="Reading installed version..." Foreground="#B195FF" Margin="0,8"/>
<TextBlock Text="Connect a trusted PC Insight release feed to check for updates. The app downloads and verifies the package, then installs it when you choose Install and restart. Results and recovery records stay on this PC." Margin="0,8"/>
<TextBlock Text="Release feed URL (HTTPS)" Foreground="#B0B5CC"/><TextBox Name="UpdateFeed" MinHeight="42" IsReadOnly="False" TextWrapping="NoWrap" ToolTip="Only use a release host you trust. Its updates run code on your PC."/>
<WrapPanel Margin="0,10"><Button Name="CheckUpdate" Content="Save feed and check"/><Button Name="DownloadUpdate" Content="Download update" IsEnabled="False"/><Button Name="InstallUpdate" Content="Install and restart" IsEnabled="False"/><Button Name="CancelUpdate" Content="Cancel download/check" IsEnabled="False"/></WrapPanel>
<TextBlock Name="LastUpdateCheck" Text="Not checked in this session." Foreground="#929BB5" Margin="0,6"/>
<TextBlock Text="Release notes" FontSize="18" Margin="0,12,0,6"/><TextBox Name="ReleaseNotes" Text="Check for updates to read what changed." Height="150" IsReadOnly="True" TextWrapping="Wrap" VerticalScrollBarVisibility="Auto"/>
<TextBlock Name="UpdateStatus" Text="Not connected: a release host must be configured before updates are available." Foreground="#B195FF"/>
<TextBlock Text="This preview is unsigned. HTTPS and SHA-256 verify transport and file integrity; they do not provide an independent publisher signature. No background checks or automatic hardware changes." Foreground="#929BB5" Margin="0,18"/>
</StackPanel></ScrollViewer></TabItem>
   <TabItem Header="Optimize my PC" Tag="&#xE945;"><ScrollViewer VerticalScrollBarVisibility="Auto"><StackPanel Margin="20">
<TextBlock Text="Guided GPU optimization" FontSize="26" FontWeight="SemiBold"/>
<TextBlock Text="1. Check compatibility   /   2. Baseline   /   3. Review change   /   4. Retest   /   5. Decide" Foreground="#B195FF" Margin="0,12"/>
<Border Name="GuideStatusCard" Style="{StaticResource Card}"><StackPanel>
<TextBlock Text="WORKFLOW STATUS" Foreground="#929BB5" FontSize="11" FontWeight="SemiBold"/>
<TextBlock Name="GuideStage" Text="Ready to begin" FontSize="23" FontWeight="SemiBold"/>
<TextBlock Name="GuideNextAction" Foreground="#EFF0FA" FontSize="15"/>
<TextBlock Name="GuideDevice" Margin="0,8" Foreground="#D8C8FF"/>
<TextBlock Name="GuideMessage" Foreground="#B0B5CC" FontSize="12"/>
</StackPanel></Border>
<TextBlock Text="This workflow tries a 90% NVIDIA power ceiling. It runs three baseline GPU tests, pauses for your approval, then applies and verifies the change and runs three retests. Allow about five minutes of testing plus review time. Higher game FPS is not guaranteed." Foreground="#B0B5CC" Margin="0,10"/>
<WrapPanel><Button Name="GuideDetect" Content="1. Check compatibility"/><Button Name="GuideBaseline" Content="2. Run baseline" IsEnabled="False"/><Button Name="GuideApply" Content="3. Review, apply and retest" IsEnabled="False"/></WrapPanel>
<WrapPanel><Button Name="GuideKeep" Content="Keep current limit" IsEnabled="False"/><Button Name="GuideRestore" Content="Restore original" Background="#28233D" IsEnabled="False"/><Button Name="GuideStop" Content="Cancel / restore" Background="#28233D" IsEnabled="False"/><Button Name="GuideExport" Content="Export guided report" IsEnabled="False"/></WrapPanel>
<TextBlock Name="GuideRecovery" Foreground="#D8C8FF" Margin="0,10"/>
<Border Style="{StaticResource Card}" Margin="0,12,12,14"><StackPanel>
<TextBlock Text="MEASURED RESULTS" Foreground="#929BB5" FontSize="11" FontWeight="SemiBold"/>
<TextBlock Name="GuideResultTitle" FontSize="21" FontWeight="SemiBold"/>
<UniformGrid Columns="3" Margin="0,8,0,12">
 <StackPanel Margin="0,0,12,0"><TextBlock Text="BASELINE MEDIAN" Foreground="#929BB5" FontSize="11"/><TextBlock Name="GuideBeforeScore" Text="--" FontSize="24" FontWeight="SemiBold" Margin="0,2"/><TextBlock Text="draws/s" Foreground="#929BB5" FontSize="12"/></StackPanel>
 <StackPanel Margin="0,0,12,0"><TextBlock Text="RETEST MEDIAN" Foreground="#929BB5" FontSize="11"/><TextBlock Name="GuideAfterScore" Text="--" FontSize="24" FontWeight="SemiBold" Margin="0,2"/><TextBlock Text="draws/s" Foreground="#929BB5" FontSize="12"/></StackPanel>
 <StackPanel><TextBlock Text="MEDIAN CHANGE" Foreground="#929BB5" FontSize="11"/><TextBlock Name="GuideChange" Text="--" FontSize="24" FontWeight="SemiBold" Foreground="#D8C8FF" Margin="0,2"/><TextBlock Text="descriptive comparison" Foreground="#929BB5" FontSize="12"/></StackPanel>
</UniformGrid>
<TextBlock Name="GuideRecommendationLabel" Text="TEST RECOMMENDATION" Foreground="#B195FF" FontSize="11" FontWeight="SemiBold"/>
<TextBlock Name="GuideRecommendation" FontSize="15"/>
<TextBlock Text="Three runs per setting. A small change or overlapping score ranges does not establish a performance benefit. Shader throughput is measured in draws/s, not game FPS." Foreground="#929BB5" FontSize="12"/>
<Expander Header="Full comparison details" Foreground="#EFF0FA" Margin="0,10,0,0" HorizontalContentAlignment="Stretch"><TextBox Name="GuideVerdict" MinHeight="160" MaxHeight="420" Margin="0,8,0,0"/></Expander>
</StackPanel></Border>
<TextBlock Text="Cancellation or a failed retest attempts restoration. A crash may require restoration on the next launch. No automatic startup writes, clock changes or voltage changes. Peak power is not energy use; three-run comparisons are descriptive, not stability certification." Foreground="#929BB5" Margin="0,14"/>
</StackPanel></ScrollViewer></TabItem>
   <TabItem Header="Game overlay" Tag="&#xE7F4;"><ScrollViewer VerticalScrollBarVisibility="Auto"><StackPanel Margin="20">
<TextBlock Text="Your game, three readings." FontSize="26" FontWeight="SemiBold"/>
<TextBlock Text="CPU temperature, GPU temperature and FPS in a small, click-through panel. Keep PC Insight open or minimized while playing." Foreground="#B0B5CC" Margin="0,8,0,20"/>
<Border Style="{StaticResource Card}"><StackPanel>
<TextBlock Text="Ctrl + Alt + O" FontSize="28" FontWeight="SemiBold" Foreground="#D8C8FF"/>
<CheckBox Name="EnableOverlayHotkey" Content="Enable this hotkey while PC Insight is open" Foreground="#EFF0FA" FontSize="15" Margin="0,12,0,18"/>
<WrapPanel><Button Name="ToggleOverlay" Content="Show overlay"/></WrapPanel>
<TextBlock Name="OverlayStatus" Text="Overlay off. Enable the hotkey, focus your game and press Ctrl+Alt+O." Foreground="#B0B5CC"/>
<TextBlock Name="LastFpsCapture" Text="No game capture yet." Foreground="#929BB5" FontSize="12"/>
<WrapPanel><Button Name="ExportFpsDetails" Content="Export FPS details" Background="#28233D" IsEnabled="False"/></WrapPanel>
</StackPanel></Border>
<TextBlock Text="Use windowed or borderless mode; exclusive fullscreen may hide the panel. The overlay follows the foreground app and appears on that screen. Press the hotkey again to stop capture and hide it." Foreground="#B0B5CC"/>
<TextBlock Text="Missing readings show --. If temperatures or FPS are unavailable, try Reopen as administrator. CPU shows the highest reported CPU temperature; GPU max means the hottest GPU core when more than one GPU reports a reading." Foreground="#929BB5"/>
<TextBlock Text="FPS is the app presentation rate over about two seconds, not a benchmark score or a count of generated/displayed frames. It may be unavailable in some games. The overlay pauses for PC Insight tests, tuning actions and updates. No game files are modified." Foreground="#929BB5"/>
</StackPanel></ScrollViewer></TabItem>
   <TabItem Header="About" Tag="&#xE897;"><DockPanel Margin="20"><StackPanel DockPanel.Dock="Top" Margin="0,0,0,16"><Image Name="AboutLogo" Source="{DynamicResource PCInsightLogo}" MaxWidth="420" Height="140" Stretch="Uniform" HorizontalAlignment="Left" RenderOptions.BitmapScalingMode="HighQuality" AutomationProperties.Name="PC Insight"/><TextBlock Name="AboutVersion" Foreground="#B0B5CC" FontSize="14" Margin="0,4,0,12"/></StackPanel><WrapPanel DockPanel.Dock="Top"><Button Name="OpenAppFolder" Content="Open app folder"/><Button Name="OpenDataFolder" Content="Open saved data folder"/></WrapPanel><TextBox Text="PC Insight - Windows desktop preview&#10;&#10;Reads Windows hardware information using CIM. NVIDIA live utilization, temperature and power are collected when nvidia-smi is already installed in a known vendor location. GPU sensor availability depends on vendor and driver support. CPU temperature and reported clocks are read through the bundled LibreHardwareMonitorLib on the Live sensors tab. CPU, RAM copy and GPU shader benchmarks are included. The optional Game overlay shows application presentation FPS and CPU/GPU temperatures. Effective-clock analysis and definitive thermal-throttling diagnosis are not implemented.&#10;&#10;Overview scans are snapshots. Live sensors offers short recordings and continuous monitoring. Continuous sessions retain the latest 300 samples. Sampling is subject to query latency. Missing data stays unavailable. There are no population rankings or invented bottleneck scores.&#10;&#10;All processing and saved results stay on this PC. No account, telemetry upload, downloaded drivers or background service. Exported reports contain hardware models and driver versions; review before sharing.&#10;&#10;System changes include installed Windows power plans and supported NVIDIA GPU power-limit reductions and manual P0 clock offsets after review. GPU originals are saved before writes and read back after apply/restore. Closing the app does not restore settings. Use Restore previous plan for Windows power plans or Restore saved GPU limit or Restore saved clock offsets on Tuning for the corresponding GPU changes. Recovery information survives app restarts.&#10;&#10;This preview is unsigned. Hardware support varies. Administrator access alone does not guarantee readings. See README.md for setup, limitations, recovery and the development roadmap."/></DockPanel></TabItem>
  </TabControl>
  <StackPanel Grid.Row="3"><ProgressBar Name="TestProgress" Height="4" Minimum="0" Maximum="100" Foreground="#9670FF" Background="#252236" BorderThickness="0"/><TextBlock Name="ProgressLabel" Text="Ready to measure" Foreground="#929BB5" FontSize="11"/><TextBlock Name="Status" Foreground="#929BB5" Text="Ready. Check Tuning for saved settings and recovery status." Margin="0,2,0,0"/></StackPanel>
 </Grid>
